From 405e4fd4880e7bef27d6a6328765a904638c8257 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:43:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: do not fire a missile when no target was chosen

borg_attack_aux_launch() scanned the quiver and kept b_k at -1 whenever
every borg_launch_bolt() returned -1, but its 'nothing to use' guard
tested b_n < 0, which cannot be true because b_n starts at zero and
candidates only raise it.  A real (non-simulated) call therefore fell
through to the firing path: it read borg_items[-1].desc for its note,
queued the fire key, a quiver slot character computed from index -1,
and the target key.  Such calls occur through borg_has_distance_attack()
in the shot-lining flow, which runs with the simulation flag off and the
target list unfilled.  Guard on the chosen missile index instead.

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c b/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c
index 45c5d140a..60e59f8e5 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c
@@ -2136,8 +2136,9 @@ int borg_attack_aux_launch(void)
         }
     }
 
-    /* Nothing to use */
-    if (b_n < 0)
+    /* Nothing to use: no candidate missile was chosen, and b_n never goes
+     * negative once initialized to zero (candidates only raise it). */
+    if (b_k < 0)
         return 0;
 
     /* Simulation */
